{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418748-taftani-negotiations-with-djinn","id":1418748,"title":"Taftani \"negotiations\" with djinn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-17T18:20:58-07:00","id":1418748,"title":"Taftani \"negotiations\" with djinn","content":"So, HDYDT seems to describe the basic process of summoning and binding a spirit like this.<br /> <br /> - Mage prepares ritual space, and if he's not a fool and/or terminally arrogant puts up some kind of ward<br /> - Mage casts the spell that actually summons the spirit to him<br /> - Mage presents offerings, demonstrates knowledge of protocol, and hopefully shows himself to be someone worth respecting enough to bargain with (making some nebulous amount of ST-defined rolls in the process) before making an offer<br /> - Mage and spirit engage in the actual contest of wills to see if this pact works out<br /> <br /> Now, I'm trying to figure out how this sort of thing should work for a Taftani binding a djinn. As I understand it, the usual Taftani negotiating tactic with a djinn is &quot;Get in the bottle,&quot; which doesn't really fit this outline. (Or rather, they do <i>sometimes</i> actually negotiate with djinn, but it's stated to be considerably more difficult than just binding the djinn, since djinn are...understandably mistrustful of humans.)<br /> <br /> The Lost Paths book really does make it sound like a Taftani who has prepared a proper bottle with the Seal of Solomon/Suleiman in advance has everything all his own way. But then, making it <i>too</i> easy on them would make Taftani seriously overpowered. I'm not against them having <i>some</i> advantage since the djinn thing is a huge part of the Taftani tradition, but there must be some limitations.<br /> <br /> My general ideas are:<br /> - Building a proper djinn bottle isn't cheap (unless it's a super weak djinn). Acquiring the necessary materials (or discovering the precise details needed for this particular djinn, such as their true name) takes the place of obtaining offerings and such. (Perhaps binding a powerful djinn requires some pawns of Tass built into the bottle or whatever.)<br /> - The roll to actually create the bottle and inscribe the Seal properly takes the place of the roll(s) to demonstrate knowledge of protocol etc. For drama's sake, the roll to see if the mage screwed this up probably shouldn't be made until the djinn is actually present.<br /> - Then the contest of wills takes place as the Taftani tries to force the djinn into the bottle.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'd consider allowing a Taftani PC to start with the Allies background representing a djinn given to him by his teacher (which sounds like a semi-common thing per Lost Crafts), but I wouldn't want a Taftani with Spirit 4 running off to build his personal army without it taking some real effort.<br /> <br /> (Of course, a non-Taftani mage who had finished dealing with a spirit would still have a pact that he needed to uphold. I'm not sure the Taftani have any equivalent for their captured djinn, aside from &quot;be careful what orders you give, lest you learn the meaning of 'malicious compliance.'&quot; That could also be a balance issue, depending on what sort of bargains spirits normally expect.)<br /> <br /> Lost Paths makes it sound like any established Taftani is going to have quite a few djinn handy. I suspect game balance is doomed by the time a PC gets to that point, though. (I'm reminded of demon summoning in Exalted, although that was pretty easy and a lot less risky than the MtA equivalent.)<br /> <br /> Has anyone dealt with a Taftani PC doing djinn stuff? How did you handle it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11237,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","user":"Jefepato","date":". 10-17-2020, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T21:41:32-07:00","id":1419121,"title":"","content":"I've only had Taftani NPCs. And I really love them as NPCs.<br /> <br /> One thing I need to consider is how to handle their relation with my Djinn Gallain Group reimagining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}